tructure this as a YAML configuration.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12846,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12846},"output_tokens":26,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fd7ac64b-a99e-4ac6-9a4b-45481da98d79","uuid":"d20f4461-a5b9-495b-b05f-28d0c982c911"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011mgJCDF3XGM6eA2hia3c98","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"exp-011 产出第二个显著 retrieval benchmark；BH-FDR 在 α=0.05 下保留 ≥2 个 benchmark；exp-004 attention pattern 与 per-example effect 有可解释关联；exp-005 找到第 4 个架构且确认 convergence 模式。原始 framing 完全成立，冲 Main。\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA 中 ≥1 个显示显著 convergence（two-tailed p < 0.05, ρ ≤ -0.9）\"\n      - \"BH-FDR 校正后 ≥2 个 benchmark 显著（adj-p < 0.05），Bonferroni 下 ≥1 个显著\"\n      - \"exp-004 attention weight 与 helped/hurt identity 的相关 > 0.3\"\n      - \"exp-005 找到 ≥1 个额外架构（如 Mamba hybrid）且 LAMBADA convergence ρ ≤ -0.7\"\n      - \"exp-007 340M rebound 有可解释的 capacity bottleneck 故事（非随机噪声）\"\n      - \"GDN-excluded sensitivity 下 ARC-Easy 达到 p < 0.05\"\n    number_ranges:\n      exp011_best_new_rho: [-1.0, -0.9]\n      exp011_best_new_p: [0.008, 0.05]\n      n_benchmarks_BH_FDR_significant: [2, 3]\n      exp004_attn_effect_correlation: [0.3, 0.5]\n      exp005_additional_arch_lambada_rho: [-1.0, -0.7]\n      lambada_cross_arch_std_reduction_pct: [75, 85]\n      per_example_jaccard_range: [0.05, 0.12]\n      n_architectures_total: [4, 5]\n    narrative_direction: \"Task-dependent convergence claim 成立于多个 retrieval benchmark（不再依赖单一 LAMBADA），per-example divergence 在 ≥4 个架构上量化为 underspecification 的具体实例。贡献从 'analytical depth on one benchmark' 升级为 'systematic characterization across tasks and architectures'。统计故事经得住 Bonferroni，W1 完全解决。W4 通过第 4 架构 + per-example 分析的独立价值充分缓解。目标 EMNLP Main。\"\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"exp-011 产出 suggestive 但非显著的第二 benchmark（p=0.05-0.15）；BH-FDR 仅保留 LAMBADA；exp-004 有描述性 attention 差异但相关偏弱；exp-005 无额外架构或结果 mixed。需要调整 claim 强度，但 task-specificity + per-example divergence 的组合故事仍可 Findings。\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"exp-011 最佳新 benchmark ρ ≈ -0.7 至 -0.8, p ≈ 0.08-0.15（suggestive, not significant）\"\n      - \"BH-FDR 仅 LAMBADA 显著；但 LAMBADA + 新 benchmark 的 convergent direction 构成 pattern\"\n      - \"exp-004 attention-effect correlation 0.15-0.30（可描述，不足以做 strong claim）\"\n      - \"exp-005 未找到可评估的额外架构，或找到但 convergence 不显著\"\n      - \"GDN-excluded ARC-Easy 维持在 ρ=-0.9, p≈0.08（suggestive, 补充证据）\"\n      - \"exp-007 340M rebound 可部分解释但非完全清晰\"\n    number_ranges:\n      exp011_best_new_rho: [-0.8, -0.6]\n      exp011_best_new_p: [0.08, 0.20]\n      n_benchmarks_BH_FDR_significant: [1, 1]\n      exp004_attn_effect_correlation: [0.15, 0.30]\n      lambada_cross_arch_std_reduction_pct: [75, 85]\n      per_example_jaccard_range: [0.05, 0.12]\n      n_architectures_total: [3, 3]\n      n_suggestive_benchmarks_p_below_0_15: [2, 3]\n    narrative_direction: \"Claim 1 从 'task-dependent convergence' 弱化为 'convergence on retrieval-heavy tasks with suggestive evidence on related benchmarks'。LAMBADA 仍是 anchor，但通过 (a) 新 benchmark 的方向一致性（即使不显著），(b) GDN-excluded ARC-Easy 的改善，(c) principled task taxonomy 来构建 converging evidence 叙事。明确承认 Bonferroni failure，用 exact permutation p + percentile CI + 方向一致性作为论证。Claim 3 per-example divergence 成为相对更强的独立贡献。exp-004 以描述性证据出现（'attention patterns differ across architectures on affected samples'），避免 mechanistic language。目标 EMNLP Findings，honest framing。\"\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"exp-011 全部新 benchmark 无 convergence 信号（ρ > -0.5 或 p > 0.3）；LAMBADA 是孤立的单点发现且不 survive 任何多重校正；exp-004 attention pattern 无解释力（correlation < 0.15）；exp-005 无进展。核心 convergence claim 站不住脚，需要 reframe 为 per-example divergence 分析论文。\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"exp-011 所有新 benchmark ρ > -0.5 且 p > 0.25（无 convergence 信号）\"\n      - \"LAMBADA convergence 被孤立为单一 benchmark 效应，无法泛化\"\n      - \"exp-004 attention-effect correlation < 0.15（attention 分析无法解释 per-example 差异）\"\n      - \"GDN-excluded 后 LAMBADA 本身也弱化（ρ=-0.7, p=0.23）——convergence 部分依赖 GDN confound\"\n      - \"exp-005 无额外架构\"\n      - \"exp-007 340M rebound 无清晰解释（噪声不可排除）\"\n    number_ranges:\n      exp011_best_new_rho: [-0.5, 0.0]\n      exp011_best_new_p: [0.25, 1.0]\n      n_benchmarks_BH_FDR_significant: [0, 1]\n      exp004_attn_effect_correlation: [0.0, 0.15]\n      lambada_cross_arch_std_reduction_pct: [75, 85]\n      per_example_jaccard_range: [0.05, 0.12]\n      n_architectures_total: [3, 3]\n      gdn_excluded_lambada_rho: [-0.7, -0.7]\n    narrative_direction: \"放弃 convergence 作为主 claim。Reframe 为：'Per-example behavioral divergence in hybrid recurrent architectures — attention induces architecture-specific sample specialization'。核心贡献变为 Claim 3 的 per-example 分析：(a) Jaccard < 0.10 的架构特异性（strongest finding, 不依赖 convergence），(b) cross-arch Kruskal-Wallis p=0.0005 证明差异是结构化的非随机的，(c) surface features + perplexity 均无法解释（rules out trivial explanations）。LAMBADA convergence 降级为 'one-task observation' 放进 discussion，不作为 claim。Claim 2 (scale) 完全降级为 supplementary observation。新的 story spine：practitioners 选择 hybrid architecture 时需要知道 attention 对不同架构的 per-example 影响是不同的 → practical implication for ensemble design / architecture selection。仍冲 Findings——per-example characterization + underspecification framing 对 EMNLP 的 analysis track 有独立价值，但需要 20+ references 的 related work 来证明 question 的 motivated-ness。\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12846,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12846},"output_tokens":26,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fd7ac64b-a99e-4ac6-9a4b-45481da98d79","uuid":"2ca9c588-50ae-4862-a5d9-7c86f3b1909f"}
